WEBVTT

00:02.527 --> 00:19.880
[SPEAKER_02]: Evening of the Third of Wealsun, after the party returns to Monmurg on the Kosair, Gouge and Merrick are summoned to go and see Lord Jamis.

00:21.282 --> 00:25.425
[SPEAKER_02]: You actually hear the captain say, you're supposed to go see Lord Jamis so he can debrief you.

00:27.907 --> 00:41.041
[SPEAKER_02]: Jude and Paul make their way from the Royal Docks up the stairs towards the palace, leaving the two of you basically hanging out by yourself, just kind of going... Let's hit the bar.

00:41.061 --> 00:42.262
[SPEAKER_02]: No, we are hitting the bar.

00:42.282 --> 00:43.063
[SPEAKER_02]: We are hitting the bar.

00:45.563 --> 00:57.848
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay, so you walk out of the Royal District and the Royal docks back towards the Harbor District, which you're much more familiar with and comfortable with, right?

00:59.549 --> 01:07.392
[SPEAKER_02]: And actually the local barracks, the Marine barracks, seems to be happening.

01:07.532 --> 01:14.715
[SPEAKER_02]: There are a lot of people outside partying, and you haven't seen it this cherry in many, many weeks.

01:16.228 --> 01:17.049
[SPEAKER_00]: What do you guys want to do?

01:17.069 --> 01:19.951
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I'm definitely...

01:20.271 --> 01:21.092
[SPEAKER_00]: These are all my men.

01:21.112 --> 01:23.233
[SPEAKER_00]: These are all my guys here, right?

01:23.413 --> 01:27.536
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I guess a lot of my guys are still on the island, but I mean, I'm still... No, these are your guys.

01:27.556 --> 01:30.598
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, I'm familiar with... A lot of your guys died.

01:30.799 --> 01:35.222
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, but... Not your guys.

01:35.422 --> 01:41.266
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, but I mean, a lot of Marines died, but these guys are all still people I know, so let's go have a drink real quick before we hit the bar.

01:41.326 --> 01:41.667
[SPEAKER_00]: Agreed.

01:44.642 --> 01:49.245
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm assuming the occasion is us returning, but I'm just going to tap one guy on the shoulder.

01:49.345 --> 01:54.808
[SPEAKER_03]: One of the guys who's got a beer out in front, looking at the dogs, cheering, goes, Folsom!

01:55.069 --> 01:59.071
[SPEAKER_04]: I go, hey, it's a special occasion.

01:59.291 --> 02:01.733
[SPEAKER_02]: Tyrus, Owen Black came back today!

02:02.904 --> 02:03.925
[SPEAKER_02]: He was in Red Shore.

02:03.965 --> 02:04.706
[SPEAKER_02]: He smuggled.

02:05.287 --> 02:06.889
[SPEAKER_02]: He smuggled food back for us.

02:07.389 --> 02:13.216
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, he smuggled back food back for the city, but he was sure to give a couple of barrels of cider to his good friends.

02:13.736 --> 02:17.160
[SPEAKER_02]: These are not watered down, my boys, like they have been in the past weeks.

02:17.661 --> 02:19.403
[SPEAKER_02]: You can get a real drunk on with this stuff.

02:20.004 --> 02:20.624
[SPEAKER_00]: Right on.

02:20.644 --> 02:21.846
[SPEAKER_02]: Go get yourselves one.

02:23.059 --> 02:25.122
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, gotta follow orders.

02:25.523 --> 02:28.086
[SPEAKER_00]: Holin' Black, I'm assuming, is a name I would know.

02:28.527 --> 02:29.849
[SPEAKER_02]: You know Owen, kind of.

02:30.329 --> 02:37.360
[SPEAKER_02]: He's actually, yeah, well, he's actually, he used to be a Marine, he's not anymore, but he knows the waters very well.

02:37.400 --> 02:39.643
[SPEAKER_02]: He's actually a relative of Merrick's.

02:39.983 --> 02:40.703
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, okay.

02:40.763 --> 02:41.964
[SPEAKER_00]: In a way.

02:42.344 --> 02:43.784
[SPEAKER_00]: Is a bit of a pirate?

02:43.804 --> 02:46.025
[SPEAKER_00]: More of a smuggler.

02:46.265 --> 02:47.045
[SPEAKER_02]: Copy.

02:47.145 --> 02:51.746
[SPEAKER_02]: But, you know, he was a little too wild for the Marines.

02:51.766 --> 02:54.907
[SPEAKER_02]: He wasn't dishonorably discharged, but he just had bigger brains.

02:54.967 --> 02:56.707
[SPEAKER_04]: Yes, better to part ways.

02:56.767 --> 03:00.028
[SPEAKER_04]: Before I go and go get a beer, I tap the guy on the side.

03:00.468 --> 03:01.528
[SPEAKER_04]: Is Owen Black around here?

03:01.548 --> 03:02.629
[SPEAKER_04]: Is he still here?

03:02.649 --> 03:03.689
[SPEAKER_04]: At the bar!

03:04.269 --> 03:05.890
[SPEAKER_04]: Well, I would love to get a beer with him.

03:05.910 --> 03:07.390
[SPEAKER_04]: Let's go do it.

03:09.746 --> 03:15.372
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay, so you walk over, and Owen's basically sitting there telling tall tales.

03:16.012 --> 03:22.799
[SPEAKER_02]: He's got this splint on his left arm, as if he has hurt his arm in some way.

03:24.300 --> 03:26.362
[SPEAKER_02]: And you haven't seen Owen for a couple of months now.

03:26.402 --> 03:29.646
[SPEAKER_02]: In fact, I think it was wintertime when you last saw him and he was around.

03:32.538 --> 03:35.621
[SPEAKER_02]: It seems like he was kind of making himself scarce there for a bit.

03:36.122 --> 03:38.724
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't know why, but he's back to himself.

03:39.205 --> 03:45.811
[SPEAKER_02]: He's the more gregarious of him and Merrick.

03:46.152 --> 03:48.994
[SPEAKER_02]: Merrick is a little bit more serious, more duty-oriented.

03:50.015 --> 03:56.262
[SPEAKER_02]: Owen is more friendlier, more freer, with a smile and a joke and so on.

03:57.614 --> 03:59.435
[SPEAKER_02]: But he knows both of you, right?

04:00.335 --> 04:04.838
[SPEAKER_02]: So he's basically laughing at the ball when the two of you walk up.

04:07.619 --> 04:08.039
[SPEAKER_04]: What do you say?

04:09.445 --> 04:11.987
[SPEAKER_04]: Owen, long time no see, good to see ya.

04:12.168 --> 04:16.091
[SPEAKER_02]: He takes a drink and looks around and goes, Ah, Folsom, how are you, lad?

04:17.012 --> 04:17.853
[SPEAKER_02]: You're looking good.

04:17.873 --> 04:23.558
[SPEAKER_02]: And who's this giant next to you that just punches you in the arm?

04:23.778 --> 04:25.780
[SPEAKER_00]: I understand you're the one who's responsible for this.

04:26.120 --> 04:30.404
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, I am responsible for it, and you owe me greatly, especially in these dire times.

04:32.145 --> 04:34.366
[SPEAKER_00]: I definitely owe you well, for sure.

04:34.546 --> 04:38.427
[SPEAKER_02]: Not a good drink to be had in the Harbor District, if it were not for me.

04:38.447 --> 04:39.208
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

04:39.788 --> 04:41.289
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, we appreciate both.

04:41.329 --> 04:45.470
[SPEAKER_00]: How did you get past the Sahuagins coming in?

04:45.870 --> 04:50.552
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, to be honest with you, I didn't even know we were having trouble with them when I was going through the waters.

04:51.172 --> 04:51.813
[SPEAKER_02]: Where have you been?

04:51.833 --> 04:55.734
[SPEAKER_02]: A little bit here, a little bit there.

04:55.754 --> 04:57.715
[SPEAKER_02]: You know it's not good to ask me that question.

04:59.286 --> 05:00.807
[SPEAKER_00]: I understand, I understand.

05:01.728 --> 05:03.209
